      "description": "Given a per-step tropical Lipschitz constant C and an iteration count n, computes the n-fold rate C**n (which equals the ultrametric rate under the norm-faithful reconstruction functor) using binary exponentiation in O(log n) multiplications. Its logarithm n*log_base C is the corresponding valuation depth, exhibiting linear depth growth behind exponential rate.",
      "pseudocode": "function ITERATED-RATE(C, n):\n    result <- 1; baseC <- C; k <- n\n    while k > 0:\n        if k is odd: result <- result * baseC\n        baseC <- baseC * baseC\n        k <- floor(k / 2)\n    return result",
      "code": "from __future__ import annotations\n\ndef iterated_rate(C: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Iterated tropical/ultrametric Lipschitz rate C**n via fast exponentiation.\"\"\"\n    result, baseC, k = 1, C, n\n    while k > 0:\n        if k & 1:\n            result *= baseC\n        baseC *= baseC\n        k >>= 1\n    return result\n"
